From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jie Ma <mjie@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] scm_user_intf_sec: find SCM device by compatible

The SCM device node name can differ across device trees. On SA8797P the
SCM node is compatible with "qcom,scm", but scm_user_intf_sec looks for a
node named "qcom_scm" and fails to get the SCM driver data.

Find the SCM node by compatible first, then keep the existing node-name
lookup as a fallback for older device trees.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Jie Ma <mjie@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/scm_user_intf_sec.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/scm_user_intf_sec.c b/drivers/scm_user_intf_sec.c
index 86ac9b6..a9b135b 100644
--- a/drivers/scm_user_intf_sec.c
+++ b/drivers/scm_user_intf_sec.c
@@ -478,10 +478,12 @@ static int qcom_scm_get_scm_drvdata(void **scm_drvdata)
 	struct platform_device *pdev = NULL;
 	struct device_node* np = NULL;
 
-	np = of_find_node_by_name(NULL, scm_dev_name);
+	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "qcom,scm");
+	if (!np)
+		np = of_find_node_by_name(NULL, scm_dev_name);
 	if (!np)
 	{
-		pr_err("Failed to find name of scm device\n");
+		pr_err("Failed to find scm device\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
-- 
